    id: "67",
    title: "Collaboration key to Africa's hospitality workforce – Kakanfo Inn CEO",
    date: "Nov 28, 2025",
    author: "Punch Newspaper",
    excerpt:
      "The Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of Kakanfo Inn and Conference Centre, Ibadan, Oyo State, Adedamola Are, has stated that building Africa's hospitality workforce and culinary future requires a collaborative approach focusing on specialised education, celebrating local identity, embracing technology, and fostering strong public private sector partnerships.",
    content: [
      "The Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of Kakanfo Inn and Conference Centre, Ibadan, Oyo State, Adedamola Are, has stated that building Africa's hospitality workforce and culinary future requires a collaborative approach focusing on specialised education, celebrating local identity, embracing technology, and fostering strong public private sector partnerships.",
      "Are made the statement on Thursday while delivering a keynote address on the theme: \u201cBuilding Africa's hospitality workforce and culinary future\u201d during the third edition of the EKAABO Trade Show event, held at the Lekan Are Hall, Kakanfo Inn and Conference Centre, Ibadan, Oyo State.",
      "He said, \u201cIt would be difficult to speak for all 54 countries in Africa. Fortunately, I have had the privilege of living in three and visited 15 percent of the African continent and have either lived with or have friends, colleagues or former teammates from every region in Africa.",
      "\u201cBuilding Africa's hospitality workforce and culinary future requires a collaborative approach focusing on specialised education, celebrating local identity, embracing technology, and fostering strong public private sector partnerships.\u201d",
      "The Hospitality Administration alumnus of the University of Nevada, Las Vegas, United States, highlighted critical challenges facing hotels in Nigeria, which he said should be taken into consideration before dissecting the future.",
      "\u201cBefore we can dissect the future, we must talk about the critical challenges that hotels and hospitality companies face in Nigeria,\u201d Are said.",
      "He identified the challenges to include infrastructure challenges, prevalence of substandard construction and installation, and in some cases improper zoning and/or use of land, staffing, government constraints, among others.",
      "\u201cIn summary, excessive tax coupled with high energy costs and a lack of governmental support relative to roads, security, water supply will make it very difficult for investors to build new projects in a capital intensive field unless they are building in primary markets like Lagos or Abuja where the prices charged for services can alleviate the costs but it is unlikely to work in secondary and tertiary markets where many resorts and hospitality outlets could be built,\u201d Are added.",
      "According to the Chairman of Kakanfo Inn, in order to address the building of Africa's hospitality and culinary workforce for the future, the following strategies must be employed: invest in targeted vocational training, co-create industry relevant curricula, emphasise work based learning, promote local culinary identity, leverage technology, foster collaboration, enhance workforce conditions, prioritise sustainability and community, empower youth and change perceptions.",
      "He said, \u201cBy implementing these strategies, Africa can build a skilled, proud, and innovative hospitality and culinary workforce that drives economic growth and establishes a globally competitive industry.\u201d",
      "Speaking to The PUNCH at the event, the Convener of EKAABO Trade Show Movement, Mrs Toyin Odugbesan, said the third edition of the show greatly impacted the hospitality industry, adding that the movement is multisectoral, transcending hospitality.",
      "She said, \u201cEKAABO has a lot to offer. It's about tourism, travel, hospitality, art, creative, culture, heritage and trade. It's multisectoral because tourism is very broad.",
      "\u201cWe've always been discussing critical issues relating to the hospitality sector and proffering sustainable solutions. For example, today's focus is on staffing. We know that staffing is a major issue facing hospitality businesses or even major businesses.",
      "\u201cThat's why we're talking about how can we solve this problem? And we decided to bring in major stakeholders that have been in this business for a long time to talk about the way they can help out.",
      "\u201cFor the 2025 EKAABO Show, we invited Mr Adedamola Are the Chairman of Kakanfo Inn which is one of the oldest hotels. We also invited the owner of Davies Hotel, Ibadan, Mr Ayodele Ogundele who has been running Davies Hotel for over 50 years, and that's a long time.",
      "\u201cHe was able to give us a practical example of one of his staff who has been working with them for over 45 years. So it's not just about theory, but about practicals \u2013 what people have been able to achieve and how they were able to achieve it.",
      "\u201cHow can the present entrepreneurs be able to pick certain things that will help them? Because once we have the staffing right, then it means that a business can thrive since people are actually the engine that drives any business to survive.\u201d",
    ],
    image: "/images/blog/67_thumb.jpg",
